<onlyinclude>'''Collective intelligence''' is the capacity of a group or coordinated system to solve problems, make judgments or accomplish intellectual tasks using contributions from multiple participants.

== Explanation ==
A group can combine observations that no individual possesses. Averaging independent estimates sometimes improves accuracy, while collaborative problem-solving can combine complementary skills. A group can also amplify mistakes when everyone copies the same source or when disagreement is suppressed.

